# Project Prompt: Django GIS Data Explorer (SQLite Database)

Build a complete Django GIS Data Explorer application using a SQLite database.

The application must allow administrators to dynamically register, import, configure, visualize, search, cluster, and report on multiple datasets containing latitude and longitude information.

The application must be enterprise-grade, metadata-driven, highly configurable, scalable, and require zero code changes whenever new datasets are introduced.

## Primary Business Objective

Analyze multiple datasets containing latitude and longitude information, dynamically configure those datasets, identify unique non-overlapping clusters within an administrator-defined radius (default 4 KM), and generate reports that help identify high-density locations suitable for future network expansion.

## Admin Module

Create an Admin Configuration panel.

This panel controls what appears on the frontend.

Administrator should be able to register any database table.

**IMPORTANT: Every configuration created from the Admin UI must be stored inside the application's own configuration tables.**

Nothing should be hardcoded inside Django models or Python files.

The application should be completely metadata-driven.

Whenever an administrator adds or modifies a source, filter, icon, column mapping, cluster settings, or frontend visibility, it must be saved in the configuration database and reflected immediately without code changes or server restart.

For every table administrator can configure:

- Source Name
- Actual Database Table
- Display Name
- Latitude Column
- Longitude Column
- Tooltip Columns
- Popup Columns
- Filter Columns
- Icon Type
- Marker Color
- Default visibility
- Sort Order
- Enable/Disable on Frontend
- Enable/Disable in Backend
- Cluster Eligible
- Default Cluster Radius
- Source Description
- Source Category
- Created By
- Created Date
- Last Modified Date

Administrator should be able to disable a source completely.

If Backend is disabled:

- APIs must ignore the source.
- Reports must ignore the source.
- Radius search must ignore the source.

If Frontend is disabled:

- Source should not appear in filters.
- Source markers should never load.
- Existing configuration should remain in database.

## Radius Search

Very important feature.

Administrator selects which sources support radius.

Cluster Radius should NOT be hardcoded.

Administrator defines the default cluster radius from Admin.

Example:

- 4 KM
- 6 KM
- 10 KM

Default value should be configurable.

The business use-case is identifying expansion opportunities by locating dense clusters.

### STRICT BUSINESS RULE

Cluster overlapping is NOT allowed.

When cluster generation runs:

- Every point can belong to only one cluster.
- No overlapping circles.
- No duplicate project assignment.
- Once a location becomes part of one cluster it cannot belong to another cluster.
- System should always generate maximum unique clusters.
- Cluster generation algorithm should guarantee non-overlapping clusters.

This rule is mandatory.

